# REMAINING WORK — Sitewide UI Audit

The Awtsmoos renews every route until no unfinished garment can hide beneath a polished shell;
Awtsmoos.com turns discovery into ownership, ownership into correction, and correction into proof that can tell.

## Closed evidence

- Whole-site census identified 228 HTML/page entries plus native-media, form, overlay, z-index, and partially styled risk clusters.
- Social Hub communication media/composer surfaces were remediated with scoped controls and green source gates.
- Universal Chat custom audio/composer work is complete and its local suite passes 26/26.
- Comment Thread custom audio/modular contracts are complete and its local suite passes 6/6.
- Rebbe player ownership was traced correctly: playback uses a headless Audio object and visible chrome is already custom.
- Rebbe download/playlist runtime stylesheet factories were replaced by static imported modules.
- Rebbe player, playlist selection, and download stack share named layer/clearance tokens rather than five-digit z-index escalation.
- Rebbe search was decomposed into small panel/template/codec/history/action/fullscreen/result modules; result data uses safe DOM and fullscreen uses one bounded shell.
- Rebbe modal init no longer injects close-button CSS; context menus clamp to viewport geometry.
- Rebbe Track Browser no longer injects runtime CSS, no longer renders active track UI with executable innerHTML or `.onclick =`, and now uses safe factories/controllers plus scoped static CSS.
- Track toolbar action ownership was reviewed and corrected before testing so local Select/Add/Playlist actions cannot double-fire controller callbacks.
- Every touched Track Browser source is <=116 lines and parses cleanly.
- Complete current Rebbe regression suite passes 9/9 tests.

## Runtime proof state

- Rebbe main route previously returned HTTP 200 through a fresh local static server after search work.
- Preview servers in this environment frequently die between acceptance waves; post-track fresh HTTP proof must be recollected on a new port rather than assuming an old server remains healthy.
- Native Chrome screenshot/eval support has been unreliable in this agent generation, so source/test/HTTP evidence remains stronger than visual geometry evidence until tooling cooperates.

## Highest-gravity current node — Rebbe Bookshelf

### Proven discovery

- `ui/bookshelf.js` contains an active-looking runtime style factory: `document.createElement('style')` plus one compressed `style.textContent` block.
- The injected selectors include bookshelf sections, rails, cards, folders, spines, metadata, actions, and empty state.
- This is the same hidden style-ownership pattern already removed from Rebbe Search, Downloads, Playlists, and Track Browser.

### NEXT_ACTION

1. Re-check Git status for Bookshelf owner files.
2. Trace `ui/bookshelf.js` imports/callers and confirm it is live in the main entry path.
3. Read the full Bookshelf renderer and any existing static style owners.
4. Write three new Bookshelf planning phases plus a final execution plan.
5. If ownership is safe, rewrite whole files only: move visible styles into small route-local CSS modules, modernize safe DOM where needed, preserve public callbacks/API, add complete interaction/mobile/reduced-motion states, and keep every touched source <=120 lines.
6. Add focused regression tests and rerun the full Rebbe suite.
7. Start a fresh isolated static server and recollect live route proof.
8. Update this ledger and continue into Rebbe Studio.

## Rebbe Studio — next major structural wave

Loaded `styles/studio.css` still contains raw stacking values including 9999 and is already >249 lines. Any touch requires a full modular split, not a local edit. The Studio wave must audit:

- range controls;
- color controls;
- checkboxes;
- selects;
- file triggers;
- textareas;
- short-height/mobile drawer behavior;
- fixed/sticky collisions;
- raw z-index values;
- inline/generated styles;
- hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, selected, loading, and reduced-motion states.

## Other loaded Rebbe layer debt

- `styles/ui.css` still contains a raw 9999 layer.
- `styles/boot.css` contains 10000.
- `styles/main.css` contains several numeric stacking values.
- `index.html` contains inline styles for `ctx-menu` and `matrix-bg`; do not touch the large entry file casually because full-file rewrite/modular extraction is required.
- Historical root `style.css` contains many raw layers but is not loaded by the main Rebbe entry; treat it as inactive unless another real entry proves otherwise.

## Remaining sitewide native-media candidates

Verify live ownership before mutation:

- `apps/lyric-sync/index.html`
- `apps/captions/video/index.html`
- `apps/video-editor/index.html` — fresh isolated interaction acceptance still pending
- `ayin/index.html`
- `games/emojis/index.html`
- `record/index.html`
- `recorder/index.html`
- `scripts/awtsmoos/social/media/renderAsset.js`
- `scripts/awtsmoos/tts/ui.js`
- `ai/js/chatgpt/audio/audioOfferMarkup.js`

## Sitewide audit classes still open

- plain/unowned input, textarea, select, file, range, checkbox, radio, color, audio, and video controls;
- visually disconnected labels, helper text, error/loading/empty states;
- dialogs, drawers, popovers, menus, and fullscreen surfaces escaping phone or short-height viewports;
- missing hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, selected/pressed, loading, and reduced-motion states;
- accidental horizontal overflow and flex/grid children missing `min-width:0` / logical containment;
- sticky/fixed collisions and arbitrary layer escalation;
- missing viewport/safe-area behavior;
- rootless/global feature CSS and historical cascade conflicts;
- controls below a practical 44px mobile touch floor;
- partially styled regions;
- public apps/games missing from their correct public indexes.

## Verification law per remediated route

- inspect real files and Git ownership first;
- full-file source rewrites only;
- touched source <=120 lines, tab-indented, readable, and documented;
- CSS remains route/subsystem-local and statically discoverable;
- relevant controls own hover/active/focus-visible/disabled/reduced-motion states;
- mobile containment and safe-area rules are explicit;
- no new z-index war;
- no visible branded native media chrome where custom UI is intended;
- existing tests plus new focused regression contracts pass;
- fresh route-load evidence follows source/test closure.

## NEXT_ACTION

Trace and plan the live Rebbe Bookshelf subsystem now, then execute its static-style/safe-DOM upgrade before entering the larger Studio wave.
